     It you want to try this, gnomish healer is by far the most popular
choice.  Healers start with quite a bit of money, so you don't have to
spend time scrounging for it; they start with multiple potions of healing
and extra healing so can either heal when wounded or drink right away to
effectively start with extra hit points; and a gnomish character will
find most of the inhabitants of the upper mines peaceful, making it a
lot easier to reach the guaranteed temple.  Their spells won't help much
though--not enough spellcasting points at that stage.

     Another choice would be archeologist, since the starting pick-aze
lets you find gold--object detection or at least magic mapping helps--
and also to dive down by diggings holes in the floor.  That's risky
since you won't know the way back up, but pacifist isn't something for
someone who's averse to taking risks.

     Caveman seems like a particularly poor choice for this gambit.


